# Prefix `not` as the operand of `+` (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | where 1 + not x == y
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..30
  PIPELINE@0..29
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..29
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..29
        LITERAL@15..16
          LONG@15..16 "1"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        PLUS@17..18 "+"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        PREFIX_EXPR@19..29
          NOT_KW@19..22 "not"
          WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
          BIN_EXPR@23..29
            NAME_REF@23..24
              IDENT@23..24 "x"
            WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
            EQ2@25..27 "=="
            WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
            NAME_REF@28..29
              IDENT@28..29 "y"
  WHITESPACE@29..30 "\n"

error[DS0114]: `not` needs parentheses here
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from T | where 1 + not x == y
  |                    ^^^ `not` binds more loosely than `+`
  |
  = help: write it as a call to say what it negates: `not(x == y)`
  = note: without parentheses, `not` negates everything up to the next `and` or `or`
